## Writing Generic Functions

### Basic Syntax
```xiom
fn identity[T](x: T) -> T {
  return x;
}
```

### With Type Constraints
```xiom
fn smaller[T: Ord](a: T, b: T) -> T {
  if a < b { return a; }
  return b;
}
```

### Generic Functions with Multiple Params
```xiom
fn swap[T](pair: (T, T)) -> (T, T) {
  return (pair.1, pair.0);
}

fn zip_with[A, B, C](a: &Vec[A], b: &Vec[B], f: fn(A, B) -> C) -> Vec[C]
  requires: a.len() == b.len();
{
  var result = Vec[C]();
  for i in 0..a.len() {
    result.push(f(a[i], b[i]));
  }
  return result;
}
```

### Type Inference at Call Sites
```xiom
let a = identity(42);       // T inferred as Int
let b = identity("hello");  // T inferred as Str
let c = identity[Bool](true); // T explicitly Bool
```

### Generic Functions with Methods
```xiom
fn describe[T: Display](value: &T) -> Str {
  return "Value: " + value.to_str();
}
```

